    {
      "id": "ab9e20d9-0b33-448b-8221-4bf748993ee3",
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        -380
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 1300,
        "content": "## Reply to LINE messages with Claude after staff approval\n\n### Who's it for\nShops that answer customers on a LINE Official Account and want AI to draft replies, while a person still decides what is sent.\n\n### How it works\n1. Receives LINE messages by webhook, checks the LINE signature, and skips redelivered events.\n2. Instantly sends a short acknowledgment with the free reply API.\n3. Photos are described by Claude, so text and photo inquiries follow the same path.\n4. Claude sorts each inquiry into stock, store visit, or other. Stock and visit inquiries are answered from two Data Tables; other inquiries are emailed to staff.\n5. The draft is emailed to staff with Send / Don't send buttons. Only approved drafts are pushed to the customer. If nobody answers within 24 hours, staff get a reminder.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create credentials: Header Auth (Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer <channel access token>`), Crypto (Hmac Secret = channel secret), Anthropic, and Gmail.\n2. Create two Data Tables and select them in the two lookup nodes:\n   - `products`: sku, name, category, color, width_cm, price, stock, note\n   - `visit_slots`: slot_date (YYYY-MM-DD), slot_time, capacity, booked\n3. Edit the **Config** node (staff email, acknowledgment text, timezone, currency).\n4. Publish, then paste the production webhook URL into the LINE Developers console. In LINE Official Account Manager, turn Webhook on and auto-reply messages off.\n\n### Requirements\nLINE Official Account with Messaging API, Anthropic API key, Gmail. n8n must be reachable over HTTPS. Set `WEBHOOK_URL` if staff approve from a phone.\n\nAI drafts can still contain promises that are not in your data, so read each draft before you approve it.\n\n### How to customize\nChange the product categories in **Extract product category**, and the reply rules in the two draft nodes.\n\nA write-up of how this template was built and tested, with screenshots (in Japanese): https://outsidernotes.com/n8n-template-line-approval-reply/"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "23d9b4ba-819b-4f23-81df-83971f6d0e01",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -50,
        54
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 2028,
        "height": 512,
        "content": "## 1. Verify and acknowledge\nChecks the LINE signature against the raw body, splits events, skips redelivered ones, and replies with a short acknowledgment. Stickers and other message types stop here."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "823fa935-5d84-4e1b-b049-0b57f93d32bd",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2002,
        -170
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1224,
        "height": 576,
        "content": "## 2. Turn photos into text\nPhotos are downloaded from LINE and described by Claude, so both paths end in one **Inquiry** node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f6943998-96cf-4c8a-9897-babea218c6b8",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3250,
        -138
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1352,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "## 3. Look up and draft\nClaude classifies the inquiry, extracts the product type or visit date, looks it up in the Data Tables, and drafts a reply based only on the results. Other inquiries go to staff by email."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "152057b4-5843-4532-b306-071e6a71d2b2",
      "name": "Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4754,
        -138
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 872,
        "height": 704,
        "content": "## 4. Staff approval\nStaff get the draft by email. **Send** pushes it to the customer, **Don't send** stops, and no answer within the wait time sends a reminder instead."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
